    {
      "id": "1ziyz31",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Causes of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hv0tsv8",
      "content": "• Movement of tectonic plates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "53w99tl",
      "content": "• Volcanic activity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "19nh717",
      "content": "• Faulting in Earth's crust."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "thq4r37",
      "content": "• Human activities such as mining and dam construction."
    },
    {
      "id": "cigsrd2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Measurement of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "id": "mwdy2bm",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Scale</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Richter Scale</p>",
            "<p>Measures magnitude (energy released).</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mercalli Scale</p>",
            "<p>Measures intensity based on damage observed.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bra191g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Effects of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "04vwbww",
      "content": "• Damage to buildings and infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x4ugk7q",
      "content": "• Landslides and ground cracks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "djliued",
      "content": "• Tsunamis in coastal regions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o1svska",
      "content": "• Loss of life and property."
    },
    {
      "id": "dfp2y6l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Major Earthquake Zones of the World"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "P-waves (Primary) travel through solids, liquids, and gases, whereas S-waves (Secondary) can only travel through solids.",
        "The Richter Scale measures earthquake magnitude (energy released) on a logarithmic scale, while the Mercalli Scale measures intensity (damage caused).",
        "The Circum-Pacific Belt, also known as the 'Pacific Ring of Fire', accounts for the majority of global earthquake and volcanic activity."
      ],
      "id": "zq6zi6v"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2s07d0y",
      "content": "• Pacific Ring of Fire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9wxfc9v",
      "content": "• Mid-Atlantic Ridge."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nj1aq4l",
      "content": "• Himalayan belt."
    },
    {
      "id": "432pzcu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ctkcuxw",
      "content": "• Pacific Ring of Fire has the highest number of volcanoes and earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "859ye22",
      "content": "• P waves travel through solids and liquids; S waves travel only through solids."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lfi2p0z",
      "content": "• Epicenter is directly above the earthquake focus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ybwg43q",
      "content": "• Richter scale measures magnitude of earthquakes."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}